Template: xpu-smi-tui/perfmon-capability
Type: boolean
Default: true
Description: Grant xpu-smi-tui the CAP_PERFMON capability?
 With CAP_PERFMON, xpu-smi-tui reports the exact VRAM in use on Arc Pro A-series
 (i915) cards and reads each card's PCIe throughput from the CPU's own counters
 (within 1%, where the GPU driver's are 5-16% high). Without it those show as
 estimates or are left blank; nothing else is affected.
 .
 The capability is set on the /usr/bin/xpu-smi-tui file only (setcap
 cap_perfmon+ep), so the program can read system-wide performance counters
 when run by any user. It reads only the GPUs' and PCIe root ports' counters.
 It is re-applied on every upgrade and removed with the package. Change later
 with: sudo dpkg-reconfigure xpu-smi-tui
